# The runtime exclude list — what the release tarball carries and what stays out.
#
# pack-app.sh (the org's shared app-release workflow, instalador #31) reads this file
# with rsync rules anchored at the app root, and it REPLACES the packer's defaults, so
# it must list every development path itself; '!' re-include lines are refused. The
# tarball carries appinfo/, js/ and css/ (both built by the release), lib/, templates/,
# img/, certs/ (the ISP intermediate the app merges into the instance's trust anchors),
# LICENSE, README.md and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md — an install needs no build step and
# no development tree.
#
# src/ needs no re-include for src/aps: the vendored aps-common code is build input,
# bundled into js/ by the release build, and nothing at runtime reads it.
# /.* covers every dotfile and dot directory at the root, this file included:
# .github, .githooks, .gitleaks.toml, .gitignore, .htaccess (a guard for a dev
# checkout's node_modules; the tarball ships none of what it denies).
- /.*
- /src
- /tests
- /docs
- /scripts
- /CHANGELOG.md
- /openapi.json
- /AGENTS.md
- /CLAUDE.md
- /CONTEXT.md
- /Makefile
- /package.json
- /package-lock.json
- /phpunit.xml
- /phpunit.integration.xml
- /vite.config.js
- /vitest.config.js
# Sourcemaps stay out of the tarball (.gitignore's rule for the repo, this one for
# the release): they name every source path of the build machine.
- /js/*.map
- /css/*.map
